# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Email (contact form + purchase receipts)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
RESEND_API_KEY=re_your_key_here

# REQUIRED before buyers can receive receipts.
#
# Resend's shared onboarding@resend.dev sender only delivers to your own
# address. Until RESEND_FROM points at a domain you've verified, the owner
# notification still arrives but the buyer's copy will not. No email provider
# allows sending to third parties from an unverified domain — this is an
# anti-spam rule, not a Resend limitation, and it applies to PayPal and bank
# transfer orders alike.
#
# To switch it on:
#   1. resend.com/domains -> Add Domain -> awaytweaks.com
#   2. Copy the three DNS records Resend shows (DKIM, SPF, DMARC) into your
#      domain registrar's DNS panel.
#   3. Wait for Resend to show "Verified" (usually minutes, up to 48h).
#   4. Set the line below and redeploy.
# RESEND_FROM=Away Tweaks <orders@awaytweaks.com>

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stripe — card payments (RECOMMENDED)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# With these set, /checkout shows a "Card" tab (selected by default) that sends
# the buyer to Stripe's own hosted checkout page, so no card data ever touches
# this site. Leave STRIPE_SECRET_KEY blank and the Card tab disappears — PayPal
# and bank transfer keep working exactly as before.
#
#   1. dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys -> copy the *Secret* key.
#      Use the Test-mode key (sk_test_…) until you've done a full test run.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
#
#   2. The webhook is what actually records the sale and sends the receipt.
#      Without it a buyer can pay and nothing happens on your side.
#
#      Local testing — install the Stripe CLI, then:
#        stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/api/stripe/webhook
#      It prints a whsec_… secret. Paste it below and restart `npm run dev`.
#
#      Production — dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks -> Add endpoint:
#        URL:   https://www.awaytweaks.com/api/stripe/webhook
#        Event: checkout.session.completed   (that one only)
#      Then copy the endpoint's signing secret below.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
#
# ⚠ Test and live mode have SEPARATE webhook endpoints and therefore separate
# signing secrets. Using the test one in production makes every real payment
# fail signature verification. The app works out which mode it's in from the
# key prefix, so there is no STRIPE_ENV to set.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PayPal — OPTIONAL
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave these blank to handle payments manually on your phone: /checkout falls
# back to a PayPal.Me link for @CarmelaBazzi (SITE.paypalMeHandle) and you
# confirm each payment yourself from the PayPal app.
#
# Fill them in to make it automatic — the site then confirms the payment,
# emails the receipt, and records the partner attribution for commission.
# developer.paypal.com -> Apps & Credentials, with the app created under the
# PayPal account that should receive the money (@CarmelaBazzi).
# Test with Sandbox credentials first, then swap in Live and set PAYPAL_ENV=live.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=
PAYPAL_ENV=sandbox

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Orders dashboard  (/admin/orders)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED to open the dashboard — it lists customer emails, so with no
# password set the page stays shut rather than defaulting to public.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# The order ledger is stored in Postgres (Neon), provisioned through Vercel's
# Marketplace: `vercel integration add neon`. That command auto-creates
# DATABASE_URL both on Vercel and in this file when you run `vercel env pull`.
# src/lib/orders/db.ts creates the `orders` table itself on first use — there
# is nothing to migrate by hand.
# DATABASE_URL=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bank transfer
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No configuration needed — the IBAN and account holder live in
# src/content/site.ts (SITE.bank). Bank transfers cannot be confirmed
# automatically (banks provide no callback), so the buyer quotes an AWAY-XXXXXX
# reference and you match it against the account manually.
